+    Subclasses :class:`ValueError` so the existing retry/fallback paths keep
+    working, while letting analyzer nodes tell "the LLM produced junk for this
+    batch" apart from "the tool is misconfigured" (also a ``ValueError``, e.g.
+    no API key).  The former should degrade that batch to zero findings; the
+    latter must stay loud.  Before this distinction existed, a single malformed
+    payload aborted the whole scan with exit code 2 and no report artifact.
